From: YeonGyu-Kim <code.yeon.gyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 02:28:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 4259/5749] fix(shared): handle Windows rename-over-existing in
 write-file-atomically (#3222)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

On Windows, renameSync fails with EPERM/EACCES when the target file
already exists. Fall back to unlink + rename on Windows permission
errors while preserving atomic semantics on other platforms.

